[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Verification Modes in Mockito: times, never, atLeast, and atMost"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Mockito provides powerful verification capabilities to ensure your code interacts with mock objects correctly. By default, Mockito verifies that a method was called exactly once. However, real-world business logic often requires more nuanced checks, such as ensuring a method is never called, called a specific number of times, or executed within a certain frequency range."},{"order":3,"type":"heading","text":"Prerequisites and Setup"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Before using verification modes, ensure you have imported the necessary static methods from Mockito to keep your test code clean and readable."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"import static org.mockito.Mockito.*;"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Verifying Exact Invocation Counts with times()"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"The times(int wantedNumberOfInvocations) mode allows you to assert that a particular method was called an exact number of times. If the actual invocation count differs, Mockito throws a VerificationError."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"public class OrderServiceTest {
    @Test
    public void testProcessOrder() {
        EmailService emailService = mock(EmailService.class);
        OrderService orderService = new OrderService(emailService);

        orderService.checkout();

        // Verify that sendConfirmationEmail was called exactly once
        verify(emailService, times(1)).sendConfirmationEmail();
    }
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Ensuring Zero Interactions with never()"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"The never() verification mode is an alias for times(0). It is crucial when writing negative test cases, ensuring that specific error-handling or conditional methods are bypassed under certain conditions."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"@Test
public void testInvalidOrderDoesNotSendEmail() {
    EmailService emailService = mock(EmailService.class);
    OrderService orderService = new OrderService(emailService);

    orderService.cancelOrder();

    // Verify that sendConfirmationEmail was never invoked
    verify(emailService, never()).sendConfirmationEmail();
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Lower Bound Verification with atLeast() and atLeastOnce()"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Sometimes you care that a method was invoked at least a certain number of times, but additional calls do not break the functionality. Mockito provides atLeast(int min) and atLeastOnce() for this purpose."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"@Test
public void testBatchProcessing() {
    LoggerService logger = mock(LoggerService.class);
    BatchProcessor processor = new BatchProcessor(logger);

    processor.processBatch(3);

    // Verify that logInfo was called at least twice during the batch process
    verify(logger, atLeast(2)).logInfo(anyString());

    // Convenience method for atLeast(1)
    verify(logger, atLeastOnce()).logStart();
}"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Upper Bound Verification with atMost()"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"To prevent performance bottlenecks or infinite loops, you can use atMost(int max) to ensure a method is not called more than a specified threshold."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"@Test
public void testRetryMechanism() {
    ApiClient client = mock(ApiClient.class);
    RetryHandler handler = new RetryHandler(client);

    handler.executeWithRetry();

    // Verify that the API endpoint is not called more than 3 times
    verify(client, atMost(3)).connect();
}"},{"order":18,"type":"heading","text":"Summary of Verification Modes"},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"times(x): Asserts the method was called exactly x times."},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"never(): Asserts the method was never called (equivalent to times(0))."},{"order":21,"type":"bullet_point","text":"atLeastOnce(): Asserts the method was called one or more times."},{"order":22,"type":"bullet_point","text":"atLeast(x): Asserts the method was called at least x times."},{"order":23,"type":"bullet_point","text":"atMost(x): Asserts the method was called at most x times."}]
